{
  "$comment": [
    "Every Google Search Central page a rule in this tool rests on, with the",
    "'Last updated' date printed on that page and the date we read it.",
    "",
    "`node scripts/google-sources.mjs` re-reads each page, compares the date, and fails",
    "when Google has moved — so drift becomes a build failure instead of a slow lie.",
    "tools/test.mjs asserts every id under `backs` exists in the rule catalogue, so a",
    "renamed check cannot orphan its source.",
    "",
    "WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY. It is not an inventory of every universal rule, and a rule",
    "absent from it is not thereby house style — 74 of the 113 universal rules are not",
    "cited here and most of them should not be. Their authority is somewhere else and",
    "that is not a weakness: the `modules` domain answers to Astro's own docs, `perf`",
    "and image delivery to the web platform, the `og:*` tags to the Open Graph protocol,",
    "the JSON-LD shapes to schema.org, the scores to Lighthouse, and a dozen rows are the",
    "tool reporting on itself. A build that will not start is a defect on anyone's site",
    "whatever Google publishes about it.",
    "",
    "What it DOES say: where this tool encodes a rule *because Google Search behaves that",
    "way*, the page and the date are written down, and a machine re-reads them."
  ],
